frankensim-shell-assembly-options-v1
# The Esteso 1964 guitar body with its bridge wall at the drawn bridge's centre, data/instruments/geometry/
# guitar-esteso-1964-zimmer2024/shell-assembly-h12-bridge-plan-drawn.tsv (its meta row "bridge_model"). The other options are those of
# esteso-h12-g.assembly, unchanged.
window-hz 15 2000
projection-work 549755813888
reference-thickness-m 0.0025
pack spruce @body
pack rosewood guitar-rosewood-brazilian-fpl-gtr282-bremaud2011-shell.fsmatpk
pack cedar guitar-cedar-western-red-fpl-gtr282-shell.fsmatpk
# bridge-component and bridge-direction are required by the options format; they apply to `bridge X Y` rows only.
bridge-component top
bridge-direction 0 0 1
# The G string meets the bridge at its saddle crest, x = 327.67 mm in the table's frame (the plan's printed saddle
# slot, read by SilentBluff for owner order 13380): a rigid, massless arm of -9.67 mm along x from the wall's top
# edge at the string's y = 5.85 mm (wall triangle 137), along the top normal. No saddle mass or compliance is added.
bridge-triangle bridge 137 0.0 0.6011900580097972 0.3988099419902028 0 0 1 -0.00967 0 0
